    questionText: "The phase \\( h(z)=k\\big(z-2z^{1/2}\\big) \\) has a saddle where \\( h'=0 \\). Find the saddle point, verify that the steepest-descent paths leaving it are \\( z_{\\pm}(\\tau)=1-\\tau^2\\pm 2 i\\tau \\) (\\( \\tau\\ge 0 \\)), and give the parabola they trace in real form \\( x=x(y) \\) with \\( z=x+iy \\).",
